, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/380747"}}, {"reference": {"label": "23", "title": {"title": "Deconstructing Decoherence"}, "misc": ["(1996) unpublished"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Anglin, J.R."}, {"full_name": "Paz, J.P."}, {"full_name": "Zurek, W.H."}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "24", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "24", "artid": "118", "year": 1963, "page_start": "118", "journal_title": "Annals Phys."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Feynman, R."}, {"full_name": "Vernon, F."}]}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9391"}}, {"reference": {"label": "25", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "118", "artid": "1", "year": 1985, "page_start": "1", "journal_title": "Phys.Rept."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Chou, K."}, {"full_name": "Hao, Z. Su B."}, {"full_name": "Yu, L."}]}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/15102"}}, {"reference": {"label": "25", "authors": [{"full_name": "Calzetta, E."}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "25", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "35", "artid": "495", "year": 1987, "page_start": "495", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}, "misc": ["and Bei-Lok Hu"]}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/231323"}}, {"reference": {"label": "26", "misc": ["Msc. Thesis, Universidad de Buenos Aires (1996) unpublished"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Romero, L. Dávila"}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "27", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "70", "artid": "1187", "year": 1993, "page_start": "1187", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "W.H.Zurek"}, {"full_name": "S.Habib"}, {"full_name": "J.P.Paz"}]}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/32909"}}], "number_of_pages": 15, "referenced_authors_bais": ["Richard.P.Feynman.1", "A.O.Caldeira.1", "A.O.Caldera.1", "W.H.Zurek.1", "Hong.Yu.Zhang.1", "F.L.Vernon.1", "E.Calzetta.1", "Y.Y.Zhang.6", "R.Laflamme.1", "Salman.Habib.1", "H.Grabert.1", "B.l.Hao.3", "A.L.Matacz.1", "W.T.Strunz.1", "E.Joos.1", "A.J.Leggett.1", "Z.B.Su.4", "T.Yu.143", "I.C.Percival.1", "H.D.Zeh.1", "J.J.Halliwell.1", "F.C.Lombardo.1", "J.P.Paz.1", "J.R.Anglin.1", "B.L.Hu.1", "F.D.Mazzitelli.1", "Kuang.chao.Chou.1", "G.L.Ingold.1", "L.Yu.10", "W.G.Unruh.1", "P.Schramm.1"], "figures": [{"filename": "Fig1Paz.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Time dependent coefficients entering in the homogeneous terms of the master equation. The environment is described by Drude's spectral density and the initial state is of zero temperature. The time dependence (in units of the renormalized frequency) of all coefficients show an initial transient for times of the order of the cutoff time--scale. Parameters for the plot are $\\omega_o=1, w_c=100, \\gamma_0=0.01$", "source": "arxiv", "key": "ee652552e74f49c8a78341c8aec41db2", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/ee652552e74f49c8a78341c8aec41db2"}, {"filename": "Fig2Paz.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Coefficients appearing in the inhomogeneous terms of the master equation. They carry the influence of the initial correlations on the future evolution. They both become negligible after a time of the order of the cutoff time--scale. Parameters for the plot are $\\omega_o=1, w_c=100$, $\\gamma_0=0.01$", "source": "arxiv", "key": "1e4e1656a5d007b0865348567c3c5121", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/1e4e1656a5d007b0865348567c3c5121"}, {"filename": "Fig3Paz.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "The evolution of the exponent which is responsible for suppressing the interference fringes. This is $A(t)/L_0^2$ for the state considered in section 5.A and $A_{ac}(t)/L_0^2$ for the one considered in section 5.B. Both curves are almost identical showing a rapid decoherence for a time--scale of the order of $w_c$. We also see that decoherence does not grow monotonically with time but in an oscillatory fashion, with maxima when peaks have position separation and minima when the separation is in momentum. Parameters of the plot are $\\gamma_0=0.01$, $w_c=100$.", "source": "arxiv", "key": "1e9d792f0bca55cd376fe50687d92814", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/1e9d792f0bca55cd376fe50687d92814"}, {"filename": "Fig4Paz.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Separation between ``internal peaks\" and characteristic size of the ``internal fringes\". This plot shows that the sub--peaks never separate and the interference fringes between them are always unobservable. The sub--peaks form a distorted Gaussian peak which moves around as a whole. Parameters of the plot are: $\\gamma_0=.01, L_0=5$, $w_c=100$.", "source": "arxiv", "key": "fbddb9a55999c20d6402c94bbd17f5c5", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/fbddb9a55999c20d6402c94bbd17f5c5"}, {"filename": "Fig5Paz.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "The position and momentum spread for a single Gaussian peak are modified on a very short time--scale during which entropy is produced. Later, they both settle towards the equilibrium values which are $\\sigma_x^2=q_\\beta^2=.498$ and $\\sigma_p^2=p_\\beta^2=.512$. Parameters of the plot are $\\gamma_0=.01, w_c=100$.", "source": "arxiv", "key": "e70f612573b52985fe83828f1607a47f", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/e70f612573b52985fe83828f1607a47f"}], "legacy_version": "20160419225806.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "1996-12-13", "preprint_date": "1996-10", "author_count": 2, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "15 pages, RevTex, 5 figures included. Submitted to Phys. Rev. A"}], "first_author": {"affiliations_identifiers": [{"schema": "ROR", "value": "https://ror.org/0081fs513"}], "full_name": "Romero, Luciana Davila", "last_name": "Romero", "first_name": "Luciana Davila", "recid": 2586940}, "control_number": 427272, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.55.4070"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.55.4070"}], "earliest_date": "1996-10", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Romero:1996bm"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We analyze the evolution of a quantum Brownian particle starting from an initial state that contains correlations between this system and its environment. Using a path integral approach, we obtain a master equation for the reduced density matrix of the system finding relatively simple expressions for its time dependent coefficients. We examine the evolution of delocalized initial states (Schr\\\"odinger's cats) investigating the effectiveness of the decoherence process. Analytic results are obtained for an ohmic environment (Drude's model) at zero temperature."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "We analyze the evolution of a quantum Brownian particle starting from an initial state that contains correlations between this system and its environment. Using a path integral approach, we obtain a master equation for the reduced density matrix of the system finding relatively simple expressions for its time dependent coefficients. We examine the evolution of delocalized initial states (Schrödinger's cats) investigating the effectiveness of the decoherence process. Analytic results are obtained for an ohmic environment (Drude's model) at zero temperature.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "1997PhRvA..55.4070D"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-3473643"}, {"schema": "MSNET", "value": "1458860"}], "titles": [{"title": "Decoherence and initial correlations in quantum Brownian motion"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Decoherence and Initial Correlations in Quantum Brownian Motion"}], "facet_author_name": ["993991_Juan Pablo Paz", "2586940_Luciana Davila Romero"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:427272", "updated": "2025-10-01